{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011SB67qWNFPzJUpQj38eLK5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"7a172083f27035a8f20aa71fbc5e208ab07fa97a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T10:00:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"HEAD -> main\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cd6cf1fcbdab85d05529d015dfb911dfef885b84\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T08:51:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-6093: Improve support for arrow functions in expression variable extractor (#1943)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5473276ce7e70c460e15b43a27f500dc452e6aa4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T17:21:26Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v11.0.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v11.0.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"15b00cf24fe4b80e857736fa1a6bd5bcfed618af\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T11:27:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Wrap workspace in div to support WebKit browsers\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"744dd2abdf636d1fc4b3b6b163220e6995378022\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:55:54-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Framework and E2E test fixes (#1934)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Framework and E2E test fixes\\n\\n* The logout spec now gets a session of its own so it doesn't race the\\n  shared auth store.\\n* O3-5982: `getTranslationOverrides()` always settles whereas previously\\n  it could hang indefinitely.\\n* O3-5975: `useConfig()` now uses only a single suspense promise per\\n  config id and drops it when it settles, so re-renders of the same\\n  component wait on the same promise. This promise now doesn't settle\\n  until the config does.\\n* Several scripts _here only_ depend on '^build' of the framework. This\\n  is correctly reflected in the turbo setup. This only applies to esm-core.\\n* The E2E scripts don't strictly depend on `docker`\\n\\n* Simplify comment\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"854ac5602d0151f85e42a2f75e39eaae4f2b2cae\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T12:13:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Move new workspace-internal properties to an internal type\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This makes O3-6007 not into a breaking change\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"59460737c9428262e242e0d09d5283ede5392a84\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T10:07:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it's containing window (#1930)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it's containing window\\n\\nWhile I want to leave the window as the default size, it's convenient\\nfor some workspaces (like the form workspace) to have a different display\\nsize depending on the content they are displaying.\\n\\nWorkspace v1 accommodated this in a less sustainable way where a\\nworkspace could modify it's size while running. This change allows the\\nsame overriding but only on a per-workspace basis. This does not\\nintroduce a hook to programmatically control the size of the workspace.\\n\\nI also removed a CSS transition that only worked when shrinking the\\nbrowser to tablet width. It seems we're going with the workspace\\n\\\"snapping\\\" without animation, so this is just for consistency.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"64eec9de063da2b2210092c275975760b6e15714\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T15:05:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a system administration pictogram (#1932)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"14ed511092191492638b35fd6f78e9ec6c2c720b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T14:57:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Cleanup unused import; fix doc\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Chi Bong Ho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2ac95182582d6628741b70b33ea2756614d4308e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T13:55:51-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6007: Add ExportedWorkspace component (#1901)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-6007: Add ExportedWorkspace component\\n\\n* Add mocks and have the component re-render on props change.\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* prevent showing of parent workspace when child is active\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* fix callback to return registered window width\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Update packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/active-workspace-window.component.tsx\\n\\n* re-instate StoreApi export; add `void` to function call\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f8aa79f6e3c0814d0f9bf8449fb79dbe08558dd0\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T20:36:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5823: Add certainty display and blue/gray defaults to diagnosis tags (#1881)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"458c3cdfcd0b8dd8ec90d3c2651fc79a944261d6\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T20:15:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Render the page header title as a heading (#1929)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Render the page header title as a heading\\n\\nPageHeaderContent now renders the page title in an h1 instead of a p.\\n\\nWith a p, the title of every page that uses the shared page header was\\nmissing from screen-reader heading navigation. Pages that move a\\nheading-level title into PageHeaderContent, such as Reports, the OCL\\nsubscription page and Fast Data Entry, lose their only heading.\\n\\nThe h1 keeps the pageName class, and its computed font, colour,\\nmargins and box size match the old p in the app shell, so the header\\nlooks the same. The implementation name stays a p.\\n\\nThe title test now looks the title up by its level-1 heading role.\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3ae5ba8ce04628f740862fcc550e31a54d716167\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T17:08:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms (#1927)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms\\n\\nAdds four pictograms for page headers that show a bare title today:\\n\\n- CohortsPictogram (omrs-pict-cohorts) for Cohort Builder: a two-by-three\\n  grid of patients with two picked out in the darker teal.\\n- ConceptDictionaryPictogram (omrs-pict-concept-dictionary) for the OCL\\n  subscription page: an open book with an arrow coming down into it.\\n- DataEntryPictogram (omrs-pict-data-entry) for Fast Data Entry: a paper\\n  form with field lines above a keyboard.\\n- ReportsPictogram (omrs-pict-reports) for Reports: four bars of uneven\\n  height on a baseline, with the tallest one dark.\\n\\nEach is drawn to stay distinct from the existing set at 92px. Cohorts\\nuses smaller figures in a grid rather than the few large figures in\\npatients and service queues, concept dictionary is a book rather than\\nthe box in metadata export, data entry adds a keyboard so it isn't\\nanother document, and reports is the set's only chart. The drawings\\nare new. Only ideas came from Carbon's population--diagram, literature,\\nkeyboard and chart--bar pictograms, and no Carbon path data was copied.\\n\\nRegisters the SVGs, adds the ids and component exports, and adds the\\ncomponents to the styleguide mocks.\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"21f3e9179769466ecbcad21b185b07af709df9e7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T12:45:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Give Service queues its own pictogram (#1926)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replaces the artwork in service-queues.svg with a new drawing: three\\npeople standing in single file, the front one in the darker teal, with a\\nchevron showing the direction the line moves. The file was byte-for-byte\\nidentical to patients.svg, so Service queues and Patient lists showed the\\nsame picture side by side in the Home left nav.\\n\\nPatient lists keeps the existing group of people, which fits a list of\\npatients. A queue is people waiting in line for a service, so the new\\ndrawing puts them in a row instead of a group.\\n\\nThe pictogram id, registration, export and mocks are unchanged, so apps\\nusing ServiceQueuesPictogram pick up the new artwork without changes. The\\ndrawing is new: only the idea of people plus a direction came from the\\nCarbon \\\"group\\\" and \\\"player--flow\\\" pictograms, and no Carbon path data was\\ncopied.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eb2447527c3a618e776241059b4df75f7d316946\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T00:20:32+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix the global error handler tests on main\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The merge of main into #1888 dropped the shared errorShapes table and\\ninlined it into the rejection handler tests only, so the window.onerror\\ntests failed with \\\"ReferenceError: errorShapes is not defined\\\".\\n\\nThe same merge brought in the standard window.onerror signature from\\n#1894, which reads the thrown value from the fifth argument. The test\\nhelper still passed it as the first, so every shape fell through to\\n\\\"'undefined' was thrown as an error\\\".\\n\\nRestore errorShapes at module level so both handler suites share it,\\nand call window.onerror the way browsers do, with a message first and\\nthe thrown value fifth. Also trim the whitespace-only lines the merge\\nleft behind.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"57315b89fd6725e86df4a4569d2c4978c5572fcf\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T01:46:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5981: Coerce error reasons to strings before showing the error toast (#1888)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Vinay Pal\",\"authorEmail\":\"palvk334@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a4dc2b875c5d3134cf36d79e5c3dc93c63af6aa3\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T15:29:38-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) O3-6029: Remove workspace v1 (#1893)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f04bb4879b27a47660f65028c4d1f0f99956d1f8\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T13:33:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a patient documents pictogram (#1924)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c1bfbcbb06105e7ffd9b4a69556722469ac13c44\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T18:54:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions (#1922)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions\\n\\nWhen an extension mounts, we update the extension config store. This can\\nforce us to recompute configurations even where nothing has changed,\\nleading to some unnecessary render churn. This adds memoization so we\\nonly recompute an extensions config if we actually need to.\\n\\nSimilarly, when sorting extensions in a slot we were unnecessarily\\ncalculating the order using a O(n^2) algorithm. This is now swapped for\\nan O(n) version at the cost of two passes through the list of extension\\nids.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address greptile's comments\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b08937f9dc7efce523d1f7a79ef94b2e6873cec6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T14:50:20-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a loading screen and update the application error screen (#1921)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"240212209388de52b020bdad3d5760f23946e451\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T23:56:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#1892)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a624af22d5816773b91f0c7768daa69617c73c24\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T16:12:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Support authentication failures from the backend (#1918)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b9884006387560e52219b747d953cac9fca2d05f\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T21:38:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Suppress Basic auth prompts for paginated REST requests (#1906)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2f1a67586aa88f6f3b42665335334dc6163bd617\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T14:27:00-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Ensure the app shell is preloaded upfront (#1912)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d32ad77c7cbd566b93fab4ef134ac0b64b2b2885\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T20:39:44+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Declare uuid as a dependency of esm-styleguide (#1913)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T00:17:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner and error page in the body grid's app area (#1904)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner in the body grid's app area\\n\\nThe app shell appends its startup spinner to <body>, which is a grid with\\nnamed areas for the top nav, left nav, app roots and workspace. The\\nspinner had no grid area, so the browser auto-placed it in a new row\\nbelow those, in the first column. That column is sized min-content, so it\\ngrew to the spinner's width (about 84px) and pushed #omrs-apps-container\\nto the right until the spinner was removed. The new row also starts below\\nthe fold, so the spinner was never visible.\\n\\nPlacing the spinner in the appRoots area leaves the column widths alone\\nand centers the spinner in the viewport. The spinner is removed right\\nafter single-spa starts, before any page mounts into\\n#omrs-apps-container, so the two don't overlap.\\n\\nOn a cold load of /spa/system-administration this removes the two layout\\nshifts the spinner caused, one when it's added and one when it's removed.\\nCLS goes from 0.113 to 0.003 on localhost, and from 0.291 to 0.164 with\\n4x CPU throttling on a 1.6 Mbps, 150 ms RTT connection.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the loading spinner grid fix\\n\\nRecords a patch entry for @openmrs/esm-styleguide describing the spinner\\nplacement fix, matching the changeset that other merged PRs in this repo\\ninclude.\\n\\n* Place the fatal error page in the body grid's app area too\\n\\nThe shell's fatal error page had the same problem as the loading spinner.\\nrenderFatalErrorPage() appends it to <body> without a grid area, so the\\nbrowser auto-placed it in an extra row below the fold, inside the\\nmin-content left nav column, which it then widened to fit its content. On\\na real startup failure (the Intl.DurationFormat polyfill chunk failing to\\nload), users saw a blank page with only an error toast.\\n\\nThis adds the error page to the spinner's appRoots rule. min-width: 0\\nstops a long error message in the code snippet from stretching the column\\npast the viewport, the same way #omrs-apps-container does. The message\\nincludes the failed chunk's URL, so its width depends on the hostname:\\nwith a realistic hostname, a 768px-wide tablet viewport overflowed by\\n160px without it. The error page now fills the app area at tablet and\\ndesktop widths and in RTL, with the heading and Reload button in view.\\n\\nAlso updates the changeset to cover the error page.\\n\\n* Document the body grid layout\\n\\nAdds a comment above the body grid that describes its areas and explains\\nwhy anything rendered into <body> in the normal flow needs one. Without an\\narea, the browser places it in a new row below the fold, in the left nav\\ncolumn, which widens to fit it. Fixed-position containers aren't affected.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\\n\\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\\nfuture version.\\n\\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\\n\\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\\n\\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\\n\\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\\n\\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\\n\\n* More clean-up\\n\\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\\n\\n* Fixup changesets\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"bc1f1355a7c22823ee60a5710c0bd9848e0aee3c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T06:53:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Navigate should refuse non-HTTP URLs (#1898)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Validate the interpolated URL before choosing the SPA navigation path so non-HTTP URLs are rejected even when the SPA base is the root. Check interpolated return URLs after login, preserve protocol-relative URLs, and cover the navigation cases with regression tests.\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"196e5d3a91159cedef8c70d1f002e6b84157c834\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T13:40:43-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6000: Allow extensions and workspaces to access their metadata (#1899)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-6000: Allow extensions and workspaces to access their meta data\\n\\n* Update packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.component.tsx\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\n\\n* Update packages/framework/esm-extensions/src/types.ts\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\n\\n* use 'unknown' type for meta value\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8173bbe9f9938ff3202e6a8a0ea3dba4c622757c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T17:07:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a metadata export pictogram (#1891)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add a metadata export pictogram\\n\\nAdds MetadataExportPictogram, drawn in the same two-tone teal as the\\nrest of the set, for the metadata export admin page in\\nopenmrs-esm-admin-tools. That page's header currently passes an empty\\nfragment as its illustration because no pictogram fits it.\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T20:22:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\\n\\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\\nnote's own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\\n\\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it's set. We leave\\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\\nto invalidate it.\\n\\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\\nAPI docs.\\n\\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\\n\\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\\nencounter to load.\\n\\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\\n\\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\\nthey have already loaded.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9ea60732d5e57aa3f13d8f2f29654a2faf3b8996\",\"date\":\"2026-09-16T16:53:12-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Improvements to the expression evaluator (#1884)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Improvements to the expression evaluator\\n\\nSpecifically:\\n\\n* Support for nullish-coalescing operator\\n* Real short-circuiting for boolean operations\\n* Address some issues with array-style property access (e.g., obj[prop]-\\n  style expressions)\\n\\n* Address Greptile's comments\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Use correct package name for esm-expression-evaluator\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7bd8088d35fcb679b6d414241ce839db75bc09b7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-16T10:58:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Upgrade to SWR 2.5.1 (#1873)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"003926fef9be3dffb14a13c84ea65be62cc162fe\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T04:51:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Release broken parcel DOM references (#1874)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Release broken parcel DOM references\\n\\nWhen a parcel rejects during unmount, single-spa retains the parcel entry\\nin the `SKIP_IF_BROKEN` state. This can include any DOM nodes it was\\npreviously attached to. We cannot fully clean-up after single-spa, but\\nsince we control the prop object we pass to it, we can clean-up the\\n`domElement` single-spa stores there, which reduces most of the memory\\npressure this causes.\\n\\nThe cost here is that every parcel receives a copy of the props passed\\nto it so we're not modifying (and clearing!) the callers props.\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806\",\"date\":\"2026-09-11T15:55:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa\\n\\nsingle-spa's \\\"timeouts\\\" actually become `setTimeout()` calls that are\\nnot cleared, even when the event they are waiting for has already\\nhappened. The upshot of this is that pushing the 15s hard timeout for\\nlifecycles to single-spa wound up holding references to unmounted apps\\nunconditionally for 15s, even after the actual contents had unmounted.\\n\\nBy moving the hard timeouts into our framework and reverting to\\nsingle-spa's defaults, we greatly reduce the window that single-spa will\\nhold the references to its default of 3s. Short of patching single-spa,\\nthis seems like the best way we can work around this issue.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address review feedback\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T14:20:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\\n\\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\\nbasically ensuring we're using a consistent browserlist.\\n\\nThis also removes the \\\"main\\\" chunk we were generating, but which was\\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\\nloader and then the index chunk.\\n\\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\\n\\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\\n\\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\\n\\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\\n\\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Fix failing test on CI\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T11:34:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Ensure slot-specific configuration are correctly passed everywhere (#1870)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4a6381c950d0a563922510fc9e1d7de9a1bdc93b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T13:47:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Pin framework to app shell version (#1863)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"99d80d2d2086665509e83708d7aa6fa1bd694c3c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T17:00:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Improve guards in dynamic-loading to prevent duplicate requests (#1862)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d24172954e6ed691318848239e157642f6e9db5\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T15:12:05-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Make pagination functions stable references (#1861)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:46:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR overhauls the extension system's internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\\n\\nBreakages:\\n\\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store's state, but the state directly.\\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"da70f7fd6691df7db8c5739f073b08f271278381\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T17:55:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Mount all single-spa parcels in a single long-lived parcel (#1858)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e6ec8408448ca34a63fe22b310c9c3cb0006b2f1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-29T00:13:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#1860)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eef2c97e8feb401ed3f5a5951ceaca1a0418bbe9\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T15:47:12-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Import map and routes should be cached (#1855)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"512f2c87802920ff9518651dc0263b1bc3281e24\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Remove `useVisitContextStore` re-render amplification (#1859)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9523b93ac4ab9a17d097813d92ae0bd587d246e6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:05:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Match workspace scopes relative to SPA base (#1857)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:13:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a distribution-controlled version property (#1815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7\",\"date\":\"2026-08-19T14:44:46+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0 (#1841)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0\\n\\nThis bumps `@openmrs/eslint-config` to [2.1.0](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-eslint-config/releases/tag/v2.1.0) which allows `typeof import(...)` annotations in test and mock files. That lets up drop the `consistent-type-imports` disable comments from our tests. While at it, this also tightens up some mock typings: wrapper args are now typed using `Parameters<typeof...>`, the `useConfig` casts in the log tests are narrower, and a few unused imports are removed.\\n\\n* Restore behavior the lint fixes accidentally changed\\n\\nThe openmrsComponentDecorator mock in esm-react-utils lost its currying\\nwhen the component param got typed. The real API takes options first,\\nthen the component, and the mock ships in the published\\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, so the two need to match. Keep the type\\nannotation, restore the currying.\\n\\nThe Logo test fixtures are whole config objects, so cast them back to\\nConfigSchema instead of double-casting through unknown to the nested\\nlogo type.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"758b953f7e498307b1bc9ec2150f1770eab60be2\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T23:37:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5874: Handle regional locales in the change language modal (#1832)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"73b51174eb9bd5d2237b9b778be176dd90e3e36e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T03:43:54+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5800: Add a two-factor authentication page and TOTP enrollment modal (#1819)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3757bfe51779418c5e407d7b5ee4097a8104d1bb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:55:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1837)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e74cebc38240317673d4e3a07f4d4f9bd976292b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:41:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0 (#1835)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0\\n\\n2.0.0 restores @typescript-eslint/no-require-imports to error for source\\nfiles, which 1.0.0 had disabled everywhere by mistake, and raises the\\nconfig's dependency floors to validated versions.\\n\\nThe config change requires two kinds of one-line fixes. Seven\\neslint-disable comments for no-require-imports come back in the webpack,\\nrspack, and storybook tooling packages. The ESLint 9 migration in #1827\\nhad removed them as unused, which they only were because 1.0.0 had\\nwrongly turned the rule off. Six stale testing-library directives go\\naway, since eslint-plugin-testing-library moves from 7.1.1 to 7.16.2 and\\nno longer reports at those sites.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green, with zero warnings under --max-warnings 0\\nacross every lint surface including the storybook package's .storybook\\nand mocks directories.\\n\\n* Move the logout spec's afterEach hook above the test\\n\\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1.0 to 2.11.0 with the config bump,\\nand its prefer-hooks-on-top rule now warns when a hook follows test cases.\\nA top-level afterEach applies to every test in the file wherever it is\\ndeclared, so moving it above the test changes nothing at runtime and\\nclears the warning that would otherwise block lint-staged commits\\ntouching this file.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"317b83fdc89dd949503906c0a9e49ed9f1457183\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T19:10:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1833)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"812a398c1eb80f280adf14885d743eb6b52fd8ab\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T23:16:16+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Exclude the CodeSnippet copy button from the primary button override (#1821)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Carbon builds the CodeSnippet copy button as a primary button (kind\\nprimary, classes cds--copy-btn cds--copy cds--btn cds--btn--primary\\ncds--btn--icon-only) and then repaints it with a layer background. The\\nstyleguide's global .cds--btn--primary override loads after Carbon's\\n.cds--copy-btn rule and ties it on specificity, so it won on source\\norder and every CodeSnippet copy button rendered as a solid brand-teal\\nprimary button instead of Carbon's subtle layer-background icon button.\\n\\nExclude the copy button from the override using :not(:where(...)). The\\nzero-specificity :where() keeps the override selectors at (0,1,0). A\\nplain :not(.cds--copy-btn) would raise them to (0,2,0), which would\\nbeat Carbon's .cds--btn:disabled rule (0,1,1) and repaint disabled\\nprimary buttons teal.\\n\\nVerified against the compiled styleguide CSS and the built app shell\\nbundle: the copy button now gets Carbon's layer background at rest,\\nlayer-hover on hover, and Carbon's own focus outline in both light and\\ndark themes, while regular and disabled primary buttons are unchanged.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f8595293d105e86e347fa06eec866d6e3e8246f\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T01:28:36+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5849: Improve the Workspace2 unsaved-changes confirmation modal (#1823)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"040fd95c5d24bd4f6fa209f6e4c24745c76178a6\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T23:48:44+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix broken o3-docs links by adding the en-US locale prefix\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"o3-docs.openmrs.org now requires a locale prefix in its URLs. Links like\\nhttps://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/configuration-system return 404, which\\nbreaks the Check documentation workflow on every PR. This prefixes all\\no3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/ links with /en-US/, matching where the pages\\nnow resolve. Each updated URL was verified to return 200.\\n\\nAlso updates the JSDoc comments in module-config.ts and ExtensionSlot.tsx\\nthat the generated esm-framework API docs are built from, so regenerating\\nthe docs does not reintroduce the old links.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"835c522f6cda1caea67efdabd7ae44a49417827c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-27T23:01:30+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Export duration helpers from the esm-framework test mock\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The esm-framework test mock re-exports the pure date utilities from\\n@openmrs/esm-utils but omits the duration family (formatDuration,\\nformatDurationBetween, duration, and ageAsDuration), all added in\\nesm-core #1680 and shipped in v10.0.0. Any component calling one of\\nthese throws \\\"formatDurationBetween is not a function\\\" in downstream\\ntests, forcing consumers to stub the function per test file (as in\\nopenmrs-esm-patient-management #2639).\\n\\nAdd the four helpers to the existing esm-utils re-export line in both\\nmock.tsx and mock-jest.tsx. They are pure functions with the same\\ngetLocale() dependency as the already re-exported formatDate, and both\\nmock files already set window.i18next.language = 'en' and load the\\nIntl.DurationFormat polyfill via @openmrs/esm-utils/mock, so they\\nresolve with no extra setup. Also adds mock-test assertions covering\\nthe new exports.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4578a99b4325318d2eee9e99774a42dbf0d75d24\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T16:48:12+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) O3-3853: Add range selection test for OpenmrsDateRangePicker\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Follow-up to #1809, which expanded the OpenmrsDatePicker test coverage.\\nThis adds the equivalent calendar popover selection test for\\nOpenmrsDateRangePicker, asserting that picking a start and end date\\ninvokes onChange with the exact selected range.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b6df901e7c1dc4a5e54bff26e146de36fde5d9fe\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T16:47:22+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) O3-3853: Expand unit test coverage for the datepicker component (#1809)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Josephkagimu1\",\"authorEmail\":\"88326256+Josephkagimu1@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4b6331027adb9c6ad2b2e027a8e6f6d9b8f49a68\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T16:26:02+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Honor the invalid prop in OpenmrsDatePicker mocks (#1814)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f47691c121b92f4e6192dd17d918d95fff855200\",\"date\":\"2026-07-10T23:44:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Resolve workspace2 lifecycles by workspace uuid instead of stack index (#1807)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"48c58067e261c522632d2f3a1186612833efc0e0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-09T17:07:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1812)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"96af8df24344161edc148f7e59b9882da209f04c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T18:07:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1805)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9dae818f0e30d56c7f31394eda770a3c15c08a8c\",\"date\":\"2026-06-29T22:05:13+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5767: Redirect to Location header URL on session endpoint calls (#1797)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"401e227eaf324ce8d2eb6332a411a6b8e5f86067\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T10:17:39+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v10.0.0 (#1794)\",\"refs\":\"tag: v10.0.0\",\"body\":\"* (chore): Release v10.0.0\\n\\n* (chore) Update @openmrs/esm-framework peerDependency to 10.x\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Bump internal @openmrs/esm-* peerDependencies to 10.x\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Use workspace:^ for internal @openmrs/esm-* peerDependencies\\n\\nLets the published peer range track the package version automatically\\n(rewritten to ^X.Y.Z by yarn npm publish) instead of hand-bumping N.x\\neach major release.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6c6f9d29ae785c34c45e1a1cad7b418fde07677c\",\"date\":\"2026-06-08T16:40:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Prevent the shared SWR cache being torn down when a decorated component unmounts (#1793)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dbe884ebda7c342a8e03992e17695714999409b8\",\"date\":\"2026-06-05T18:01:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1792)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"26f3df2d9ce92b2a189ccfc48708d6d1b956067f\",\"date\":\"2026-06-04T19:00:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5646: Remove extra padding from NumericObs cell variant in tablet mode (#1769)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5646: Remove extra padding from NumericObs cell variant in tablet mode\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5646: Fix uneven padding on NumericObs cell variant in tablet mode\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"sfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7d84b4dddcbd16627c6e81e5052b074a25646141\",\"date\":\"2026-06-03T16:20:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove doubled heading padding in EmptyCard and ErrorState (#1790)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"317b3fa103d84de1ab5aed5c18f993555e78d812\",\"date\":\"2026-05-29T09:58:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Workspace2 is not longer experimental; deprecate currentVisit (#1781)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"10685bf0073bfa39b5a64f3d8c3d1751810b4ab4\",\"date\":\"2026-05-28T23:52:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Restore pagination container text left padding (#1783)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3cabb166c7cfcff42595488657c810b5cd350b32\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T13:20:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Add launchWorkspaceGroup2 to framework mocks\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a0c0320040097a65a08361110e0c322998e63dd2\",\"date\":\"2026-05-21T15:51:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Restore lg height for Search component (#1778)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The bundled Carbon emits the layout-token clamp on .cds--search-input\\nbut does not bridge the cds--search--lg size class to\\n--cds-layout-size-height, so <Search size=\\\"lg\\\"> falls back to md (40px)\\nand renders shorter than a paired lg Button across O3. Set the token\\non .cds--search--lg in the styleguide so the clamp resolves to lg\\n(48px) until @carbon/styles is bumped to a version that wires this\\nup natively.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"89487272bee51407cf8bf89ec897e8c42ff91c78\",\"date\":\"2026-05-20T13:46:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"fix date range separator alignment\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e1470604dafd40c0e687b75b8838278061c511db\",\"date\":\"2026-05-12T04:26:08+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5651: Update the procedure order icon (#1773)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ee754fabbb5c2c7beaa2123590cac44e0d27b1e\",\"date\":\"2026-05-07T13:45:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add matchLocale framework function (#1771)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f1c28bc93332623961245b26da6347cef223131c\",\"date\":\"2026-05-06T14:18:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Add a semi-automated documentation workflow (#1770)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e16e2d9e16a891670bbf4dd0a79ebe81414405d8\",\"date\":\"2026-05-01T18:32:38+05:30\",\"message\":\"(test) Add regression tests for 401 Location-header redirect in openmrsFetch (#1754)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ash\",\"authorEmail\":\"aishwarya.tripathi2023@vitstudent.ac.in\"},{\"hash\":\"27586f5d34c1650ad0c5a47757d7307b171c9c11\",\"date\":\"2026-04-25T00:07:29+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4924: Align expand animation and size prop with Carbon design system (#1758)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Raj Prakash\",\"authorEmail\":\"rjnt452@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"72fd6729c812247e07e0103339acea0131801898\",\"date\":\"2026-04-22T13:30:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update docs\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3a3d56ba49fd0762855e0a54ccab7c4020dda2f7\",\"date\":\"2026-04-21T17:42:39+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4020: Return current app context value synchronously on first render (#1751)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Devarasetty Praneeth\",\"authorEmail\":\"89689768+praneeth622@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f8ef2378eee546bd8eea8259922dd40408c672c\",\"date\":\"2026-04-18T16:15:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Avoid stray vertical line in OpenmrsDateRangePicker inputs (#1753)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1dcccfd421c94ee0f0a8aa6c7c974cadab3d5fb8\",\"date\":\"2026-04-15T09:22:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Drop IMO and don't load arbitrary content in production mode (#1743)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ab4238d82cc85db143aa1dd89ada2a1e7402448f\",\"date\":\"2026-04-15T07:56:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Styleguide needs to depend on `@react-aria/utils`\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ed69afd536b1027a2b230342e2f03157b872a4ea\",\"date\":\"2026-04-12T15:23:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Small optimization to runtime SVG loading (#1742)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":86}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e42b2604-3b58-4b35-8168-9634a4f84015","uuid":"f1ad1e78-54cf-4316-acf2-fb946e520049","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:45:21.210Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"7a172083f27035a8f20aa71fbc5e208ab07fa97a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T10:00:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"HEAD -> main\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"cd6cf1fcbdab85d05529d015dfb911dfef885b84\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T08:51:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-6093: Improve support for arrow functions in expression variable extractor (#1943)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5473276ce7e70c460e15b43a27f500dc452e6aa4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T17:21:26Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v11.0.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v11.0.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"15b00cf24fe4b80e857736fa1a6bd5bcfed618af\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T11:27:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Wrap workspace in div to support WebKit browsers\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"744dd2abdf636d1fc4b3b6b163220e6995378022\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:55:54-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Framework and E2E test fixes (#1934)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Framework and E2E test fixes\\n\\n* The logout spec now gets a session of its own so it doesn't race the\\n  shared auth store.\\n* O3-5982: `getTranslationOverrides()` always settles whereas previously\\n  it could hang indefinitely.\\n* O3-5975: `useConfig()` now uses only a single suspense promise per\\n  config id and drops it when it settles, so re-renders of the same\\n  component wait on the same promise. This promise now doesn't settle\\n  until the config does.\\n* Several scripts _here only_ depend on '^build' of the framework. This\\n  is correctly reflected in the turbo setup. This only applies to esm-core.\\n* The E2E scripts don't strictly depend on `docker`\\n\\n* Simplify comment\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"854ac5602d0151f85e42a2f75e39eaae4f2b2cae\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T12:13:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Move new workspace-internal properties to an internal type\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This makes O3-6007 not into a breaking change\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"59460737c9428262e242e0d09d5283ede5392a84\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T10:07:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it's containing window (#1930)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Allow a workspace to override the size of it's containing window\\n\\nWhile I want to leave the window as the default size, it's convenient\\nfor some workspaces (like the form workspace) to have a different display\\nsize depending on the content they are displaying.\\n\\nWorkspace v1 accommodated this in a less sustainable way where a\\nworkspace could modify it's size while running. This change allows the\\nsame overriding but only on a per-workspace basis. This does not\\nintroduce a hook to programmatically control the size of the workspace.\\n\\nI also removed a CSS transition that only worked when shrinking the\\nbrowser to tablet width. It seems we're going with the workspace\\n\\\"snapping\\\" without animation, so this is just for consistency.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"64eec9de063da2b2210092c275975760b6e15714\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T15:05:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a system administration pictogram (#1932)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"14ed511092191492638b35fd6f78e9ec6c2c720b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T14:57:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Cleanup unused import; fix doc\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Chi Bong Ho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2ac95182582d6628741b70b33ea2756614d4308e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T13:55:51-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6007: Add ExportedWorkspace component (#1901)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-6007: Add ExportedWorkspace component\\n\\n* Add mocks and have the component re-render on props change.\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* prevent showing of parent workspace when child is active\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* fix callback to return registered window width\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Update packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/active-workspace-window.component.tsx\\n\\n* re-instate StoreApi export; add `void` to function call\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f8aa79f6e3c0814d0f9bf8449fb79dbe08558dd0\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T20:36:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5823: Add certainty display and blue/gray defaults to diagnosis tags (#1881)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"458c3cdfcd0b8dd8ec90d3c2651fc79a944261d6\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T20:15:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Render the page header title as a heading (#1929)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Render the page header title as a heading\\n\\nPageHeaderContent now renders the page title in an h1 instead of a p.\\n\\nWith a p, the title of every page that uses the shared page header was\\nmissing from screen-reader heading navigation. Pages that move a\\nheading-level title into PageHeaderContent, such as Reports, the OCL\\nsubscription page and Fast Data Entry, lose their only heading.\\n\\nThe h1 keeps the pageName class, and its computed font, colour,\\nmargins and box size match the old p in the app shell, so the header\\nlooks the same. The implementation name stays a p.\\n\\nThe title test now looks the title up by its level-1 heading role.\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3ae5ba8ce04628f740862fcc550e31a54d716167\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T17:08:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms (#1927)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add cohorts, concept dictionary, data entry and reports pictograms\\n\\nAdds four pictograms for page headers that show a bare title today:\\n\\n- CohortsPictogram (omrs-pict-cohorts) for Cohort Builder: a two-by-three\\n  grid of patients with two picked out in the darker teal.\\n- ConceptDictionaryPictogram (omrs-pict-concept-dictionary) for the OCL\\n  subscription page: an open book with an arrow coming down into it.\\n- DataEntryPictogram (omrs-pict-data-entry) for Fast Data Entry: a paper\\n  form with field lines above a keyboard.\\n- ReportsPictogram (omrs-pict-reports) for Reports: four bars of uneven\\n  height on a baseline, with the tallest one dark.\\n\\nEach is drawn to stay distinct from the existing set at 92px. Cohorts\\nuses smaller figures in a grid rather than the few large figures in\\npatients and service queues, concept dictionary is a book rather than\\nthe box in metadata export, data entry adds a keyboard so it isn't\\nanother document, and reports is the set's only chart. The drawings\\nare new. Only ideas came from Carbon's population--diagram, literature,\\nkeyboard and chart--bar pictograms, and no Carbon path data was copied.\\n\\nRegisters the SVGs, adds the ids and component exports, and adds the\\ncomponents to the styleguide mocks.\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"21f3e9179769466ecbcad21b185b07af709df9e7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T12:45:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Give Service queues its own pictogram (#1926)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replaces the artwork in service-queues.svg with a new drawing: three\\npeople standing in single file, the front one in the darker teal, with a\\nchevron showing the direction the line moves. The file was byte-for-byte\\nidentical to patients.svg, so Service queues and Patient lists showed the\\nsame picture side by side in the Home left nav.\\n\\nPatient lists keeps the existing group of people, which fits a list of\\npatients. A queue is people waiting in line for a service, so the new\\ndrawing puts them in a row instead of a group.\\n\\nThe pictogram id, registration, export and mocks are unchanged, so apps\\nusing ServiceQueuesPictogram pick up the new artwork without changes. The\\ndrawing is new: only the idea of people plus a direction came from the\\nCarbon \\\"group\\\" and \\\"player--flow\\\" pictograms, and no Carbon path data was\\ncopied.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eb2447527c3a618e776241059b4df75f7d316946\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T00:20:32+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Fix the global error handler tests on main\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The merge of main into #1888 dropped the shared errorShapes table and\\ninlined it into the rejection handler tests only, so the window.onerror\\ntests failed with \\\"ReferenceError: errorShapes is not defined\\\".\\n\\nThe same merge brought in the standard window.onerror signature from\\n#1894, which reads the thrown value from the fifth argument. The test\\nhelper still passed it as the first, so every shape fell through to\\n\\\"'undefined' was thrown as an error\\\".\\n\\nRestore errorShapes at module level so both handler suites share it,\\nand call window.onerror the way browsers do, with a message first and\\nthe thrown value fifth. Also trim the whitespace-only lines the merge\\nleft behind.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"57315b89fd6725e86df4a4569d2c4978c5572fcf\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T01:46:53+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5981: Coerce error reasons to strings before showing the error toast (#1888)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Vinay Pal\",\"authorEmail\":\"palvk334@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a4dc2b875c5d3134cf36d79e5c3dc93c63af6aa3\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T15:29:38-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) O3-6029: Remove workspace v1 (#1893)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f04bb4879b27a47660f65028c4d1f0f99956d1f8\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T13:33:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a patient documents pictogram (#1924)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c1bfbcbb06105e7ffd9b4a69556722469ac13c44\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T18:54:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions (#1922)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions\\n\\nWhen an extension mounts, we update the extension config store. This can\\nforce us to recompute configurations even where nothing has changed,\\nleading to some unnecessary render churn. This adds memoization so we\\nonly recompute an extensions config if we actually need to.\\n\\nSimilarly, when sorting extensions in a slot we were unnecessarily\\ncalculating the order using a O(n^2) algorithm. This is now swapped for\\nan O(n) version at the cost of two passes through the list of extension\\nids.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address greptile's comments\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b08937f9dc7efce523d1f7a79ef94b2e6873cec6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T14:50:20-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a loading screen and update the application error screen (#1921)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"240212209388de52b020bdad3d5760f23946e451\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T23:56:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#1892)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a624af22d5816773b91f0c7768daa69617c73c24\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T16:12:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Support authentication failures from the backend (#1918)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b9884006387560e52219b747d953cac9fca2d05f\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T21:38:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Suppress Basic auth prompts for paginated REST requests (#1906)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2f1a67586aa88f6f3b42665335334dc6163bd617\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T14:27:00-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Ensure the app shell is preloaded upfront (#1912)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d32ad77c7cbd566b93fab4ef134ac0b64b2b2885\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T20:39:44+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Declare uuid as a dependency of esm-styleguide (#1913)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T00:17:38+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner and error page in the body grid's app area (#1904)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner in the body grid's app area\\n\\nThe app shell appends its startup spinner to <body>, which is a grid with\\nnamed areas for the top nav, left nav, app roots and workspace. The\\nspinner had no grid area, so the browser auto-placed it in a new row\\nbelow those, in the first column. That column is sized min-content, so it\\ngrew to the spinner's width (about 84px) and pushed #omrs-apps-container\\nto the right until the spinner was removed. The new row also starts below\\nthe fold, so the spinner was never visible.\\n\\nPlacing the spinner in the appRoots area leaves the column widths alone\\nand centers the spinner in the viewport. The spinner is removed right\\nafter single-spa starts, before any page mounts into\\n#omrs-apps-container, so the two don't overlap.\\n\\nOn a cold load of /spa/system-administration this removes the two layout\\nshifts the spinner caused, one when it's added and one when it's removed.\\nCLS goes from 0.113 to 0.003 on localhost, and from 0.291 to 0.164 with\\n4x CPU throttling on a 1.6 Mbps, 150 ms RTT connection.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the loading spinner grid fix\\n\\nRecords a patch entry for @openmrs/esm-styleguide describing the spinner\\nplacement fix, matching the changeset that other merged PRs in this repo\\ninclude.\\n\\n* Place the fatal error page in the body grid's app area too\\n\\nThe shell's fatal error page had the same problem as the loading spinner.\\nrenderFatalErrorPage() appends it to <body> without a grid area, so the\\nbrowser auto-placed it in an extra row below the fold, inside the\\nmin-content left nav column, which it then widened to fit its content. On\\na real startup failure (the Intl.DurationFormat polyfill chunk failing to\\nload), users saw a blank page with only an error toast.\\n\\nThis adds the error page to the spinner's appRoots rule. min-width: 0\\nstops a long error message in the code snippet from stretching the column\\npast the viewport, the same way #omrs-apps-container does. The message\\nincludes the failed chunk's URL, so its width depends on the hostname:\\nwith a realistic hostname, a 768px-wide tablet viewport overflowed by\\n160px without it. The error page now fills the app area at tablet and\\ndesktop widths and in RTL, with the heading and Reload button in view.\\n\\nAlso updates the changeset to cover the error page.\\n\\n* Document the body grid layout\\n\\nAdds a comment above the body grid that describes its areas and explains\\nwhy anything rendered into <body> in the normal flow needs one. Without an\\narea, the browser places it in a new row below the fold, in the left nav\\ncolumn, which widens to fit it. Fixed-position containers aren't affected.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\\n\\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\\nfuture version.\\n\\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\\n\\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\\n\\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\\n\\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\\n\\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\\n\\n* More clean-up\\n\\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\\n\\n* Fixup changesets\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"bc1f1355a7c22823ee60a5710c0bd9848e0aee3c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T06:53:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Navigate should refuse non-HTTP URLs (#1898)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Validate the interpolated URL before choosing the SPA navigation path so non-HTTP URLs are rejected even when the SPA base is the root. Check interpolated return URLs after login, preserve protocol-relative URLs, and cover the navigation cases with regression tests.\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"196e5d3a91159cedef8c70d1f002e6b84157c834\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T13:40:43-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-6000: Allow extensions and workspaces to access their metadata (#1899)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-6000: Allow extensions and workspaces to access their meta data\\n\\n* Update packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.component.tsx\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\n\\n* Update packages/framework/esm-extensions/src/types.ts\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\n\\n* use 'unknown' type for meta value\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8173bbe9f9938ff3202e6a8a0ea3dba4c622757c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T17:07:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a metadata export pictogram (#1891)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Add a metadata export pictogram\\n\\nAdds MetadataExportPictogram, drawn in the same two-tone teal as the\\nrest of the set, for the metadata export admin page in\\nopenmrs-esm-admin-tools. That page's header currently passes an empty\\nfragment as its illustration because no pictogram fits it.\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T20:22:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\\n\\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\\nnote's own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\\n\\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it's set. We leave\\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\\nto invalidate it.\\n\\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\\nAPI docs.\\n\\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\\n\\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\\nencounter to load.\\n\\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\\n\\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\\nthey have already loaded.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9ea60732d5e57aa3f13d8f2f29654a2faf3b8996\",\"date\":\"2026-09-16T16:53:12-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Improvements to the expression evaluator (#1884)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Improvements to the expression evaluator\\n\\nSpecifically:\\n\\n* Support for nullish-coalescing operator\\n* Real short-circuiting for boolean operations\\n* Address some issues with array-style property access (e.g., obj[prop]-\\n  style expressions)\\n\\n* Address Greptile's comments\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Use correct package name for esm-expression-evaluator\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7bd8088d35fcb679b6d414241ce839db75bc09b7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-16T10:58:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Upgrade to SWR 2.5.1 (#1873)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"003926fef9be3dffb14a13c84ea65be62cc162fe\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T04:51:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Release broken parcel DOM references (#1874)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Release broken parcel DOM references\\n\\nWhen a parcel rejects during unmount, single-spa retains the parcel entry\\nin the `SKIP_IF_BROKEN` state. This can include any DOM nodes it was\\npreviously attached to. We cannot fully clean-up after single-spa, but\\nsince we control the prop object we pass to it, we can clean-up the\\n`domElement` single-spa stores there, which reduces most of the memory\\npressure this causes.\\n\\nThe cost here is that every parcel receives a copy of the props passed\\nto it so we're not modifying (and clearing!) the callers props.\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806\",\"date\":\"2026-09-11T15:55:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa\\n\\nsingle-spa's \\\"timeouts\\\" actually become `setTimeout()` calls that are\\nnot cleared, even when the event they are waiting for has already\\nhappened. The upshot of this is that pushing the 15s hard timeout for\\nlifecycles to single-spa wound up holding references to unmounted apps\\nunconditionally for 15s, even after the actual contents had unmounted.\\n\\nBy moving the hard timeouts into our framework and reverting to\\nsingle-spa's defaults, we greatly reduce the window that single-spa will\\nhold the references to its default of 3s. Short of patching single-spa,\\nthis seems like the best way we can work around this issue.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address review feedback\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T14:20:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\\n\\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\\nbasically ensuring we're using a consistent browserlist.\\n\\nThis also removes the \\\"main\\\" chunk we were generating, but which was\\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\\nloader and then the index chunk.\\n\\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\\n\\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\\n\\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\\n\\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\\n\\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Fix failing test on CI\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T11:34:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Ensure slot-specific configuration are correctly passed everywhere (#1870)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4a6381c950d0a563922510fc9e1d7de9a1bdc93b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T13:47:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Pin framework to app shell version (#1863)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"99d80d2d2086665509e83708d7aa6fa1bd694c3c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T17:00:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Improve guards in dynamic-loading to prevent duplicate requests (#1862)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d24172954e6ed691318848239e157642f6e9db5\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T15:12:05-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Make pagination functions stable references (#1861)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:46:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR overhauls the extension system's internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\\n\\nBreakages:\\n\\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store's state, but the state directly.\\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"da70f7fd6691df7db8c5739f073b08f271278381\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T17:55:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Mount all single-spa parcels in a single long-lived parcel (#1858)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e6ec8408448ca34a63fe22b310c9c3cb0006b2f1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-29T00:13:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#1860)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eef2c97e8feb401ed3f5a5951ceaca1a0418bbe9\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T15:47:12-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Import map and routes should be cached (#1855)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"512f2c87802920ff9518651dc0263b1bc3281e24\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Remove `useVisitContextStore` re-render amplification (#1859)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9523b93ac4ab9a17d097813d92ae0bd587d246e6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:05:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Match workspace scopes relative to SPA base (#1857)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:13:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a distribution-controlled version property (#1815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5d184f007ca88666efaf7d276c0cafa9450736c7\",\"date\":\"2026-08-19T14:44:46+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0 (#1841)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.1.0\\n\\nThis bumps `@openmrs/eslint-config` to [2.1.0](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-eslint-config/releases/tag/v2.1.0) which allows `typeof import(...)` annotations in test and mock files. That lets up drop the `consistent-type-imports` disable comments from our tests. While at it, this also tightens up some mock typings: wrapper args are now typed using `Parameters<typeof...>`, the `useConfig` casts in the log tests are narrower, and a few unused imports are removed.\\n\\n* Restore behavior the lint fixes accidentally changed\\n\\nThe openmrsComponentDecorator mock in esm-react-utils lost its currying\\nwhen the component param got typed. The real API takes options first,\\nthen the component, and the mock ships in the published\\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, so the two need to match. Keep the type\\nannotation, restore the currying.\\n\\nThe Logo test fixtures are whole config objects, so cast them back to\\nConfigSchema instead of double-casting through unknown to the nested\\nlogo type.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"758b953f7e498307b1bc9ec2150f1770eab60be2\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T23:37:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5874: Handle regional locales in the change language modal (#1832)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"73b51174eb9bd5d2237b9b778be176dd90e3e36e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T03:43:54+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5800: Add a two-factor authentication page and TOTP enrollment modal (#1819)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3757bfe51779418c5e407d7b5ee4097a8104d1bb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:55:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1837)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e74cebc38240317673d4e3a07f4d4f9bd976292b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:41:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0 (#1835)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0\\n\\n2.0.0 restores @typescript-eslint/no-require-imports to error for source\\nfiles, which 1.0.0 had disabled everywhere by mistake, and raises the\\nconfig's dependency floors to validated versions.\\n\\nThe config change requires two kinds of one-line fixes. Seven\\neslint-disable comments for no-require-imports come back in the webpack,\\nrspack, and storybook tooling packages. The ESLint 9 migration in #1827\\nhad removed them as unused, which they only were because 1.0.0 had\\nwrongly turned the rule off. Six stale testing-library directives go\\naway, since eslint-plugin-testing-library moves from 7.1.1 to 7.16.2 and\\nno longer reports at those sites.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green, with zero warnings under --max-warnings 0\\nacross every lint surface including the storybook package's .storybook\\nand mocks directories.\\n\\n* Move the logout spec's afterEach hook above the test\\n\\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1.0 to 2.11.0 with the config bump,\\nand its prefer-hooks-on-top rule now warns when a hook follows test cases.\\nA top-level afterEach applies to every test in the file wherever it is\\ndeclared, so moving it above the test changes nothing at runtime and\\nclears the warning that would otherwise block lint-staged commits\\ntouching this file.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"317b83fdc89dd949503906c0a9e49ed9f1457183\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T19:10:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1833)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"812a398c1eb80f280adf14885d743eb6b52fd8ab\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T23:16:16+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Exclude the CodeSnippet copy button from the primary button override (#1821)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Carbon builds the CodeSnippet copy button as a primary button (kind\\nprimary, classes cds--copy-btn cds--copy cds--btn cds--btn--primary\\ncds--btn--icon-only) and then repaints it with a layer background. The\\nstyleguide's global .cds--btn--primary override loads after Carbon's\\n.cds--copy-btn rule and ties it on specificity, so it won on source\\norder and every CodeSnippet copy button rendered as a solid brand-teal\\nprimary button instead of Carbon's subtle layer-background icon button.\\n\\nExclude the copy button from the override using :not(:where(...)). The\\nzero-specificity :where() keeps the override selectors at (0,1,0). A\\nplain :not(.cds--copy-btn) would raise them to (0,2,0), which would\\nbeat Carbon's .cds--btn:disabled rule (0,1,1) and repaint disabled\\nprimary buttons teal.\\n\\nVerified against the compiled styleguide CSS and the built app shell\\nbundle: the copy button now gets Carbon's layer background at rest,\\nlayer-hover on hover, and Carbon's own focus outline in both light and\\ndark themes, while regular and disabled primary buttons are unchanged.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f8595293d105e86e347fa06eec866d6e3e8246f\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T01:28:36+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5849: Improve the Workspace2 unsaved-changes confirmation modal (#1823)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"040fd95c5d24bd4f6fa209f6e4c24745c76178a6\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T23:48:44+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix broken o3-docs links by adding the en-US locale prefix\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"o3-docs.openmrs.org now requires a locale prefix in its URLs. Links like\\nhttps://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/configuration-system return 404, which\\nbreaks the Check documentation workflow on every PR. This prefixes all\\no3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/ links with /en-US/, matching where the pages\\nnow resolve. Each updated URL was verified to return 200.\\n\\nAlso updates the JSDoc comments in module-config.ts and ExtensionSlot.tsx\\nthat the generated esm-framework API docs are built from, so regenerating\\nthe docs does not reintroduce the old links.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"835c522f6cda1caea67efdabd7ae44a49417827c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-27T23:01:30+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Export duration helpers from the esm-framework test mock\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The esm-framework test mock re-exports the pure date utilities from\\n@openmrs/esm-utils but omits the duration family (formatDuration,\\nformatDurationBetween, duration, and ageAsDuration), all added in\\nesm-core #1680 and shipped in v10.0.0. Any component calling one of\\nthese throws \\\"formatDurationBetween is not a function\\\" in downstream\\ntests, forcing consumers to stub the function per test file (as in\\nopenmrs-esm-patient-management #2639).\\n\\nAdd the four helpers to the existing esm-utils re-export line in both\\nmock.tsx and mock-jest.tsx. They are pure functions with the same\\ngetLocale() dependency as the already re-exported formatDate, and both\\nmock files already set window.i18next.language = 'en' and load the\\nIntl.DurationFormat polyfill via @openmrs/esm-utils/mock, so they\\nresolve with no extra setup. Also adds mock-test assertions covering\\nthe new exports.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4578a99b4325318d2eee9e99774a42dbf0d75d24\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T16:48:12+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) O3-3853: Add range selection test for OpenmrsDateRangePicker\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Follow-up to #1809, which expanded the OpenmrsDatePicker test coverage.\\nThis adds the equivalent calendar popover selection test for\\nOpenmrsDateRangePicker, asserting that picking a start and end date\\ninvokes onChange with the exact selected range.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b6df901e7c1dc4a5e54bff26e146de36fde5d9fe\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T16:47:22+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) O3-3853: Expand unit test coverage for the datepicker component (#1809)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Josephkagimu1\",\"authorEmail\":\"88326256+Josephkagimu1@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4b6331027adb9c6ad2b2e027a8e6f6d9b8f49a68\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T16:26:02+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Honor the invalid prop in OpenmrsDatePicker mocks (#1814)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f47691c121b92f4e6192dd17d918d95fff855200\",\"date\":\"2026-07-10T23:44:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Resolve workspace2 lifecycles by workspace uuid instead of stack index (#1807)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"48c58067e261c522632d2f3a1186612833efc0e0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-09T17:07:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1812)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"96af8df24344161edc148f7e59b9882da209f04c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T18:07:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1805)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9dae818f0e30d56c7f31394eda770a3c15c08a8c\",\"date\":\"2026-06-29T22:05:13+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5767: Redirect to Location header URL on session endpoint calls (#1797)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"401e227eaf324ce8d2eb6332a411a6b8e5f86067\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T10:17:39+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v10.0.0 (#1794)\",\"refs\":\"tag: v10.0.0\",\"body\":\"* (chore): Release v10.0.0\\n\\n* (chore) Update @openmrs/esm-framework peerDependency to 10.x\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Bump internal @openmrs/esm-* peerDependencies to 10.x\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Use workspace:^ for internal @openmrs/esm-* peerDependencies\\n\\nLets the published peer range track the package version automatically\\n(rewritten to ^X.Y.Z by yarn npm publish) instead of hand-bumping N.x\\neach major release.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6c6f9d29ae785c34c45e1a1cad7b418fde07677c\",\"date\":\"2026-06-08T16:40:57+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Prevent the shared SWR cache being torn down when a decorated component unmounts (#1793)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dbe884ebda7c342a8e03992e17695714999409b8\",\"date\":\"2026-06-05T18:01:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#1792)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"26f3df2d9ce92b2a189ccfc48708d6d1b956067f\",\"date\":\"2026-06-04T19:00:37+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5646: Remove extra padding from NumericObs cell variant in tablet mode (#1769)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5646: Remove extra padding from NumericObs cell variant in tablet mode\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5646: Fix uneven padding on NumericObs cell variant in tablet mode\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"sfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7d84b4dddcbd16627c6e81e5052b074a25646141\",\"date\":\"2026-06-03T16:20:07+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove doubled heading padding in EmptyCard and ErrorState (#1790)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"317b3fa103d84de1ab5aed5c18f993555e78d812\",\"date\":\"2026-05-29T09:58:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Workspace2 is not longer experimental; deprecate currentVisit (#1781)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"10685bf0073bfa39b5a64f3d8c3d1751810b4ab4\",\"date\":\"2026-05-28T23:52:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Restore pagination container text left padding (#1783)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3cabb166c7cfcff42595488657c810b5cd350b32\",\"date\":\"2026-05-26T13:20:39+03:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Add launchWorkspaceGroup2 to framework mocks\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a0c0320040097a65a08361110e0c322998e63dd2\",\"date\":\"2026-05-21T15:51:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Restore lg height for Search component (#1778)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The bundled Carbon emits the layout-token clamp on .cds--search-input\\nbut does not bridge the cds--search--lg size class to\\n--cds-layout-size-height, so <Search size=\\\"lg\\\"> falls back to md (40px)\\nand renders shorter than a paired lg Button across O3. Set the token\\non .cds--search--lg in the styleguide so the clamp resolves to lg\\n(48px) until @carbon/styles is bumped to a version that wires this\\nup natively.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"89487272bee51407cf8bf89ec897e8c42ff91c78\",\"date\":\"2026-05-20T13:46:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"fix date range separator alignment\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e1470604dafd40c0e687b75b8838278061c511db\",\"date\":\"2026-05-12T04:26:08+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5651: Update the procedure order icon (#1773)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ee754fabbb5c2c7beaa2123590cac44e0d27b1e\",\"date\":\"2026-05-07T13:45:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add matchLocale framework function (#1771)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f1c28bc93332623961245b26da6347cef223131c\",\"date\":\"2026-05-06T14:18:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Add a semi-automated documentation workflow (#1770)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e16e2d9e16a891670bbf4dd0a79ebe81414405d8\",\"date\":\"2026-05-01T18:32:38+05:30\",\"message\":\"(test) Add regression tests for 401 Location-header redirect in openmrsFetch (#1754)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ash\",\"authorEmail\":\"aishwarya.tripathi2023@vitstudent.ac.in\"},{\"hash\":\"27586f5d34c1650ad0c5a47757d7307b171c9c11\",\"date\":\"2026-04-25T00:07:29+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4924: Align expand animation and size prop with Carbon design system (#1758)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Raj Prakash\",\"authorEmail\":\"rjnt452@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"72fd6729c812247e07e0103339acea0131801898\",\"date\":\"2026-04-22T13:30:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update docs\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3a3d56ba49fd0762855e0a54ccab7c4020dda2f7\",\"date\":\"2026-04-21T17:42:39+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-4020: Return current app context value synchronously on first render (#1751)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Devarasetty Praneeth\",\"authorEmail\":\"89689768+praneeth622@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f8ef2378eee546bd8eea8259922dd40408c672c\",\"date\":\"2026-04-18T16:15:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Avoid stray vertical line in OpenmrsDateRangePicker inputs (#1753)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1dcccfd421c94ee0f0a8aa6c7c974cadab3d5fb8\",\"date\":\"2026-04-15T09:22:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Drop IMO and don't load arbitrary content in production mode (#1743)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ab4238d82cc85db143aa1dd89ada2a1e7402448f\",\"date\":\"2026-04-15T07:56:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Styleguide needs to depend on `@react-aria/utils`\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ed69afd536b1027a2b230342e2f03157b872a4ea\",\"date\":\"2026-04-12T15:23:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Small optimization to runtime SVG loading (#1742)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"