{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QuPgUU76YUkheL1brUbEg5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"744dd2abdf636d1fc4b3b6b163220e6995378022\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:55:54-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Framework and E2E test fixes (#1934)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Framework and E2E test fixes\\n\\n* The logout spec now gets a session of its own so it doesn't race the\\n  shared auth store.\\n* O3-5982: `getTranslationOverrides()` always settles whereas previously\\n  it could hang indefinitely.\\n* O3-5975: `useConfig()` now uses only a single suspense promise per\\n  config id and drops it when it settles, so re-renders of the same\\n  component wait on the same promise. This promise now doesn't settle\\n  until the config does.\\n* Several scripts _here only_ depend on '^build' of the framework. This\\n  is correctly reflected in the turbo setup. This only applies to esm-core.\\n* The E2E scripts don't strictly depend on `docker`\\n\\n* Simplify comment\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c1bfbcbb06105e7ffd9b4a69556722469ac13c44\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T18:54:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions (#1922)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions\\n\\nWhen an extension mounts, we update the extension config store. This can\\nforce us to recompute configurations even where nothing has changed,\\nleading to some unnecessary render churn. This adds memoization so we\\nonly recompute an extensions config if we actually need to.\\n\\nSimilarly, when sorting extensions in a slot we were unnecessarily\\ncalculating the order using a O(n^2) algorithm. This is now swapped for\\nan O(n) version at the cost of two passes through the list of extension\\nids.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address greptile's comments\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T11:34:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Ensure slot-specific configuration are correctly passed everywhere (#1870)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:46:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR overhauls the extension system's internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\\n\\nBreakages:\\n\\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store's state, but the state directly.\\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"040fd95c5d24bd4f6fa209f6e4c24745c76178a6\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T23:48:44+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix broken o3-docs links by adding the en-US locale prefix\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"o3-docs.openmrs.org now requires a locale prefix in its URLs. Links like\\nhttps://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/configuration-system return 404, which\\nbreaks the Check documentation workflow on every PR. This prefixes all\\no3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/ links with /en-US/, matching where the pages\\nnow resolve. Each updated URL was verified to return 200.\\n\\nAlso updates the JSDoc comments in module-config.ts and ExtensionSlot.tsx\\nthat the generated esm-framework API docs are built from, so regenerating\\nthe docs does not reintroduce the old links.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":6}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e42b2604-3b58-4b35-8168-9634a4f84015","uuid":"552c5863-8937-4404-b68f-847e80d055e8","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:45:27.772Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"744dd2abdf636d1fc4b3b6b163220e6995378022\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:55:54-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Framework and E2E test fixes (#1934)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Framework and E2E test fixes\\n\\n* The logout spec now gets a session of its own so it doesn't race the\\n  shared auth store.\\n* O3-5982: `getTranslationOverrides()` always settles whereas previously\\n  it could hang indefinitely.\\n* O3-5975: `useConfig()` now uses only a single suspense promise per\\n  config id and drops it when it settles, so re-renders of the same\\n  component wait on the same promise. This promise now doesn't settle\\n  until the config does.\\n* Several scripts _here only_ depend on '^build' of the framework. This\\n  is correctly reflected in the turbo setup. This only applies to esm-core.\\n* The E2E scripts don't strictly depend on `docker`\\n\\n* Simplify comment\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c1bfbcbb06105e7ffd9b4a69556722469ac13c44\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T18:54:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions (#1922)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Minimize churn from config updates when there are many extensions\\n\\nWhen an extension mounts, we update the extension config store. This can\\nforce us to recompute configurations even where nothing has changed,\\nleading to some unnecessary render churn. This adds memoization so we\\nonly recompute an extensions config if we actually need to.\\n\\nSimilarly, when sorting extensions in a slot we were unnecessarily\\ncalculating the order using a O(n^2) algorithm. This is now swapped for\\nan O(n) version at the cost of two passes through the list of extension\\nids.\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Address greptile's comments\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2864290a3797a6a581958d2d89cd00be08fe8c2d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T11:34:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Ensure slot-specific configuration are correctly passed everywhere (#1870)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9042cb6c5010ab2316aeec2dc295bf4c410a66de\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:46:10-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Extension system should not re-derive in full on every write (#1856)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This PR overhauls the extension system's internal recomputation model to eliminate O(n²) behavior where any single write triggered a full re-derivation of state for every module, extension, and slot in the app.\\n\\nBreakages:\\n\\n* assignedExtensions in the extension store are renamed candidateExtensions to reflect their role. Use getAssignedExtensions() or useAssignedExtensions() to get the correct list.\\n* useAssignedExtensionIds() is now implemented in terms of useAssignedExtensions() and has been deprecated.\\n* useStore() no longer returns a copy of the store's state, but the state directly.\\n* Parcels will hard fail if they do not render within 15 seconds of loading.\\n* Extensions added through configuration now retain the order they are defined in configuration.\\n* Extension rendering state is no longer tracked in the extension store.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"040fd95c5d24bd4f6fa209f6e4c24745c76178a6\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T23:48:44+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix broken o3-docs links by adding the en-US locale prefix\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"o3-docs.openmrs.org now requires a locale prefix in its URLs. Links like\\nhttps://o3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/configuration-system return 404, which\\nbreaks the Check documentation workflow on every PR. This prefixes all\\no3-docs.openmrs.org/docs/ links with /en-US/, matching where the pages\\nnow resolve. Each updated URL was verified to return 200.\\n\\nAlso updates the JSDoc comments in module-config.ts and ExtensionSlot.tsx\\nthat the generated esm-framework API docs are built from, so regenerating\\nthe docs does not reintroduce the old links.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":6}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QuPgUU76YUkheL1brUbEg5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
